  "errors": [],
  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "In Limited formats, choosing to be on the play is almost always correct. Being on the play gives you tempo advantage — you get to play lands and threats first, which is critical in Limited where board presence matters most. Choosing to draw (letting the opponent go first) gives you an extra card but sacrifices the tempo advantage, which is generally not worth it unless you have a very specific control deck that wants the extra card.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to be on the draw (selected opponent as starting player)",
      "better_line": "Choose to be on the play (select yourself as starting player) to gain tempo advantage, which is the default correct choice in Limited.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 1,
      "player": "Kimi25 Valley",
      "decision_index": 0,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Mulliganed a strong 7-card hand that had 3 lands, a powerful curve (Turn 2 Hero's Blade, Turn 4 Balan auto-equipping for a 6/5 first strike), and a backup plan with Soulcage Fiend and Kothophed. The only weakness was having just 1 Swamp for BB costs, but the primary game plan (Hero's Blade + Balan) only needs Plains.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to mulligan to 6 cards",
      "better_line": "Keep the 7-card hand. Hero's Blade into Balan is an extremely strong synergy that's castable with the available mana, and 3 lands is a fine starting count.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "MiMo Coach",
      "decision_index": 1,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Bottomed the only Swamp (black mana source) instead of a redundant Plains. The hand has 3 Plains which already covers the white mana costs for all spells in hand (Honor Guard, Chains of Custody, Kwende). The 4th land (Swamp) provides crucial access to the deck's second color for any black spells drawn later.",
      "action_taken": "Bottomed the Swamp, leaving hand with 3 Plains and no black mana source",
      "better_line": "Bottom a Plains instead, keeping 2 Plains + 1 Swamp (or even 3 Plains + 1 Swamp if keeping 4 lands). This maintains access to black mana while still curving out perfectly with the white spells in hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 3,
      "player": "MiMo Coach",
      "decision_index": 3,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Swamp instead of Thriving Isle on turn 2. Thriving Isle enters tapped, and with only 2 mana available this turn, there's nothing to cast anyway. Playing the tapped land now means it's untapped on turn 3 for a 3-drop (Wavebreak Hippocamp, Infernal Idol, or even Vendilion Clique with flash). Playing Swamp now forces Thriving Isle to come in tapped on turn 3, losing a full turn of tempo on 3-drops.",
      "action_taken": "Played Swamp (untapped land) on turn 2 with no 2-mana plays available.",
      "better_line": "Play Thriving Isle (choosing black) on turn 2 so it enters tapped now and is available untapped on turn 3, enabling a turn-3 three-drop.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 12,
      "player": "Kimi25 Valley",
      "decision_index": 6,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Timed out on Thriving Isle color choice. The deck is UB with multiple black-heavy cards in hand (Skullslither Worm, Strangling Spores, Yargle). Black is clearly the correct choice to have a dual-color land producing both Blue and Black. The timeout likely defaulted to a useless color like White, making the Thriving Isle effectively a worse Island for the rest of the game.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out, getting a default color choice (likely White) instead of actively choosing.",
      "better_line": "Choose Black for Thriving Isle to have access to both Blue and Black mana, supporting the heavy black requirements in hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 31,
      "player": "Kimi25 Valley",
      "decision_index": 9,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With no castable spells this turn (Chains of Custody has no valid target since opponent controls no nonland permanents, and Kwende costs 4), the extra untapped mana from Swamp is wasted. Thriving Moor entering tapped costs nothing this turn and provides better color flexibility (can choose white for an extra white source).",
      "action_taken": "Played Swamp (untapped) when there were no 3-mana plays available this turn.",
      "better_line": "Play Thriving Moor (choosing white) since it enters tapped at no cost when you have no plays, saving Swamp for a future turn when entering untapped matters.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 38,
      "player": "MiMo Coach",
      "decision_index": 12,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to attack with Benalish Honor Guard into an empty board with no blockers and no untapped mana on the opponent's side. This is 2 free damage that was left on the table.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and did not declare any attackers.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Benalish Honor Guard for 2 unblockable damage against the empty board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 41,
      "player": "MiMo Coach",
      "decision_index": 13,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Cast Chains of Custody when the opponent has no nonland permanents on the battlefield, meaning the exile ETB trigger has no valid target and does nothing. This wastes one of the best white removal spells in limited just to give a 2/2 ward {2}.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Chains of Custody on Benalish Honor Guard with no opponent nonland permanents to exile",
      "better_line": "Hold Chains of Custody for when the opponent plays actual threats to exile. Could pass the turn and save it for a meaningful target later.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 48,
      "player": "MiMo Coach",
      "decision_index": 14,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to cast Fleeting Distraction as a cantrip when there was a legal target (Benalish Honor Guard) and no other meaningful use for the mana this turn. With 2 available mana and nothing else castable, drawing a card for U would have been free value to help dig toward lands and playable spells.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting Fleeting Distraction",
      "better_line": "Cast Fleeting Distraction targeting Benalish Honor Guard to draw a card, since there's no better use for the U mana this turn and the hand needs to find land drops to deploy expensive threats like Yargle and Skullslither Worm.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 59,
      "player": "Kimi25 Valley",
      "decision_index": 16,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Playing Thriving Moor (which enters tapped) instead of Plains or Swamp means only 3 mana is available this turn, delaying Kwende, Pride of Femeref by a full turn. Kwende is a powerful 2/2 double striker that also gives Benalish Honor Guard +1/+0 (legendary synergy), making it a 3/2. Getting Kwende down a turn earlier is significant tempo.",
      "action_taken": "Played Thriving Moor (enters tapped), leaving only 3 mana available this turn.",
      "better_line": "Play Plains (or Swamp) to have 4 mana available and immediately cast Kwende, Pride of Femeref this turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 63,
      "player": "MiMo Coach",
      "decision_index": 17,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to cast Fleeting Distraction when having 1 blue mana available and no other use for it this turn. With a hand full of expensive cards (4+ mana) and only 3 lands in play, drawing a card to potentially find a land was valuable. No meaningful spells could be cast with the remaining mana regardless.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting Fleeting Distraction",
      "better_line": "Cast Fleeting Distraction targeting Benalish Honor Guard to draw a card and dig toward lands. The U mana would otherwise go unused, and finding a 4th land is critical for deploying threats like Skullslither Worm next turn. Alternatively, saving it for the opponent's combat to reduce Honor Guard's damage by 1 while drawing is also reasonable, but the land-finding urgency favors casting now.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 65,
      "player": "Kimi25 Valley",
      "decision_index": 19,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to attack with Benalish Honor Guard (2/2) into an empty board. The opponent has no creatures, so this is 2 free damage with zero risk.",
      "action_taken": "Timed out and did not declare attackers",
      "better_line": "Attack with Benalish Honor Guard for 2 unblockable damage against an empty board.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 66,
      "player": "MiMo Coach",
      "decision_index": 20,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to cast Fleeting Distraction on the attacking Benalish Honor Guard. Fleeting Distraction would reduce 2 damage to 1 damage and draw a card, all for just {U}. This is essentially free value — save 1 life and cantrip. The only argument for holding it is to later trigger Wavebreak Hippocamp's draw ability on the opponent's turn, but Hippocamp isn't in play yet and the immediate guaranteed value of saving life while cantripping is better than speculative future synergy.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, taking 2 damage from Benalish Honor Guard instead of 1",
      "better_line": "Cast Fleeting Distraction targeting Benalish Honor Guard to save 1 life and draw a card for {U}",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 70,
      "player": "Kimi25 Valley",
      "decision_index": 21,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Kwende before playing a land drop. Playing Plains or Swamp first (both enter untapped) would give 5 mana total, allowing Kwende to be cast with 1 mana remaining open, which is strictly better than using all 4 available mana on Kwende and then playing a land with nothing to spend it on.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Kwende, Pride of Femeref with all 4 available mana before making the land drop.",
      "better_line": "Play Plains (or Swamp) first, then cast Kwende, Pride of Femeref, leaving 1 mana open for potential interaction or flexibility.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 87,
      "player": "MiMo Coach",
      "decision_index": 25,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Plains instead of Swamp when the only spell in hand is Infernal Idol, which has a {1}{B}{B} activated ability. Swamp would better support both casting the Idol (generic cost) and eventually activating it.",
      "action_taken": "Played Plains as the land drop",
      "better_line": "Play Swamp to have better access to {B}{B} for Infernal Idol's sacrifice ability (would have 2 Swamps + Thriving Moor for 3 black sources)",
      "type": "blunder",
