      "decision_index": 27,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Kimi25 Valley declined to attack with Wavebreak Hippocamp into a board where the only possible blocker is Kwende (2/2, just entered). If opponent doesn't block, it's 2 free damage. If opponent blocks with Kwende, Kimi25 can use Fleeting Distraction to shrink Kwende to 1/2, win combat, draw a card, AND remove the dangerous double strike lord. Either outcome is favorable.",
      "action_taken": "Did not attack with Wavebreak Hippocamp.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Wavebreak Hippocamp. If Kwende blocks, use Fleeting Distraction to win combat and draw a card. If Kwende doesn't block, deal 2 damage for free.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 116,
      "player": "Kimi25 Valley",
      "decision_index": 33,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Infernal Idol before playing a land drop. Should always play the land first to maximize available mana after casting spells, as there's no reason to hold the land. Playing Swamp first would leave 3 mana open after casting Infernal Idol instead of 2.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Infernal Idol with land drop still unused",
      "better_line": "Play Swamp first, then cast Infernal Idol, leaving 3 mana open instead of 2",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 120,
      "player": "MiMo Coach",
      "decision_index": 34,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "MiMo Coach timed out and failed to declare any attackers when they had a dominant board position. Kwende (2/2 double strike) and Benalish Honor Guard (3/2) could attack into a single Wavebreak Hippocamp (2/2) with all opponent's lands tapped. Any block scenario results in the Hippocamp dying while MiMo Coach's creatures survive, dealing 3-7 damage to a 13-life opponent. Missing this attack wastes a massive combat step.",
      "action_taken": "No response - failed to declare any attackers",
      "better_line": "Attack with all. In every blocking scenario, Hippocamp dies (Kwende's first strike or Honor Guard's 3 power kills it) and MiMo Coach deals 3-7 damage while losing nothing. This pressures the opponent significantly at 13 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 129,
      "player": "MiMo Coach",
      "decision_index": 36,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Took 7 damage (going from 13 to 6 life) by not blocking, when blocking Benalish Honor Guard with Wavebreak Hippocamp would have traded the Hippocamp for the Honor Guard and saved 3 life (going to 10 instead). At 6 life, Kimi25 Valley is in serious danger. While Wavebreak Hippocamp has ongoing value for drawing cards off instant-speed spells, the life total is too precarious to justify preserving it over a profitable trade.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to block, taking 7 damage (3 from Honor Guard + 4 from Kwende's double strike) to drop to 6 life.",
      "better_line": "Block Benalish Honor Guard with Wavebreak Hippocamp to trade 2/2 for the 3/2 Honor Guard, taking only 4 damage from Kwende (going to 9 life) while removing a threat.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 133,
      "player": "Kimi25 Valley",
      "decision_index": 37,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "With opponent's creatures all tapped, Kimi25 Valley should play Swamp and cast Yargle (9/3) to attack into the defenseless board for 9 damage, bringing opponent to 11. Strangling Spores could be saved for the opponent's turn to get a Wavebreak Hippocamp draw trigger. Instead, they used the removal spell precombat when there was no immediate threat (all opponent creatures tapped) and missed a huge attack opportunity.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Strangling Spores in precombat main phase when opponent's creatures were tapped",
      "better_line": "Play Swamp, cast Yargle Glutton of Urborg (9/3) for 4B, attack for 9 damage into tapped-out board, save Strangling Spores for opponent's turn to trigger Wavebreak Hippocamp card draw",
      "type": "blunder",
